= Senator Garm Bel Iblis of Corellia

Brilliant, stubborn and suspicious of everyone, Corellia’s senator believes democracy has to be defended, if necessary with turbolasers. He trusts no Chancellor.

[? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : *Our advisors can act again in [+ advisor_action_timer +] turn(s).* ?]

- @bel_iblis_corsec: Strengthen Corellian Security.
- @bel_iblis_security: Work the Security Bloc.
- @bel_iblis_denounce: Denounce corruption from the floor.
- @go_back: Back.

@bel_iblis_corsec
subtitle: +0.6 member-world forces; calms the Hawks.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: Our advisors have already acted recently.
on-arrival: member_forces += 0.6; hawk_dissent -= 6; advisor_action_timer = 5

Bel Iblis quietly arranges for CorSec to share training and equipment with the security forces of other Caucus worlds.

@bel_iblis_security
subtitle: +8 relations with the Security Bloc.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: Our advisors have already acted recently.
on-arrival: sec_relation += 8; advisor_action_timer = 5

The Security Bloc respects strength. Bel Iblis gives them a long talk about it.

@bel_iblis_denounce
subtitle: −2 corruption, more support in the Core; the Commerce Guilds are furious.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: Our advisors have already acted recently.
on-arrival: corruption -= 2; core_rc += 1.5; guild_relation -= 6; advisor_action_timer = 5

Bel Iblis names names. The galleries erupt. The trade guilds will not forget this.
